:{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur\/bezierOffset2","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslur\/bezieroffset2","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bezierOffset2","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur with a continue type. Deprecated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bezierX2"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"bezierOffset2","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDivisions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The divisions type is used to express values in terms of the musical divisions defined by the divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. It is preferred that these be integer values both for MIDI interoperability and to avoid roundoff"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"errors."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldivisions","title":"MXLDivisions"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSlur":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSlur","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSlur","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slur types are empty. Most slurs are represented with two elements: one with a start type, and one with a stop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type. Slurs can add more elements using a continue type. This is typically used to specify the formatting of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cross-system slurs, or to specify the shape of very complex slurs."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlslur","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSlur","title":"MXLSlur","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}